    ("jamb_eng_2012_82", "English Language", "Grammar and Structure", "2012", "__ your parents frown __ [A. Because / over B. Since / at C. Although / at D. As / upon] our friendship, we shouldn’t see each other anymore.", "Because / over", "Since / at", "Although / at", "As / upon", 1, "Subordinating causal clause 'Since' followed by the preposition 'frown at'."),
